issueContext.body:
Walking through a couple scenarios of how users would go about promoting their resources with the introduction of compatibility version. Feature gates are self explanatory via versioned_kube_features.go but resource APIs are a bit different. 

We determine the resources we serve based on the emulation version https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/master/pkg/controlplane/apiserver/apis.go#L91. Alpha APIs are disabled by default, and not compatible with emulation version so we can omit them from the current discussion. Beta APIs are also disabled by default, but is something we want to capture in emulation version. GA APIs are enabled by default, and is definitely something we want to capture in emulation version.

Promoting an API from alpha to beta and from beta to GA yields certain cases that need to be handled with emulation version.

User stories will be from the perspective of a feature developer. 

## User Story 1 : Promoting an API from alpha to beta.

Somewhere in the apiserver I have something like 

```go
// v1.31
if featuregate.Enabled(MyFeature) {
   r := &v1alpha1.MyType{}
   // operations on the resource
}
```

Once the feature goes beta, the traditional workflow will change the code to something like 

```go
// v1.32
if featuregate.Enabled(MyFeature) {
  // alpha resource directly replaced with beta resource on new version
   r := &v1beta1.MyType{}
   // operations on the resource
}
```

This is fine because we do not allow [alpha APIs to be enabled along with emulation version](https://github.com/kubernetes/enhancements/blob/master/keps/sig-architecture/4330-compatibility-versions/README.md#api-availability).  Thus, 1.32 can emulate 1.31 but `MyFeature` cannot be enabled, and despite not knowing about how to handle the alpha type when emulating 1.31, the code path will never be exercised. 

